# Jupiter Converse Batching

## Invariant

`∀ Cursor seat · multi-stop Jupiter bus-nudge: prefer ≤3 turns per --converse session` (operator bind 2026-07-16; friction 24831). **Soft ceiling** — not a hard lock; 1-turn OK for a single ask; >3 only with a named reason.

Substance + exemptions: Use the `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` skill § Converse batching.

## Quick bind

| Situation | Action |
|---|---|
| Meaning walk / multi-stop ping-pong with next 1–2 stops known | One `--converse` with 2–3 `--prompt-file` turns |
| Single gated ask (e.g. life-advisor position) | One turn is fine |
| Operator gate or craft mode next | New session; do not batch across the gate |
| Whole remaining queue | Prefer batches of ≤3; open another converse for the rest |

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| One Jupiter session per Stop on a known multi-stop queue | Prefer ≤3 Stops per converse |
| Re-acquire CDP lane for every web reply cycle | Keep the warm converse for the batch |
| Pack Attachment A craft into the meaning-walk nudge | Separate converse for craft |
| Treating 3 as a hard reject of a 4th useful turn | Exceed only with a named reason |
